Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 14:12:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(conport): restore migration foundation gate
 (clobbered by #932) + ledger hardening
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR #917 merged the operator-gated ConPort migration foundation gate to main
(c45b2c8e7, 19:58Z). PR #932 ("Palette: Team Dashboard", 559d7e2fa, 20:12Z) was
based on pre-#917 main and its merge reverted #917 wholesale — removing the gate
and its tests and restoring enhanced_server.py/schema.sql to their pre-#917
state (re-enabling hidden startup ALTERs). No Palette content touched those
ConPort files; it was a stale-branch clobber.

This restores #917's gate at its canonical path
(docker/mcp-servers-source/conport/migrations/conport_migration_gate.py), its
wiring (Dockerfile COPY migrations, enhanced_server.py operator-gating,
schema.sql, migrations 004/007/README), tests, proof bundle, and task packet,
returning main to the operator-gated design.

It also ports the unique ledger-safety hardening from the twin PR #928 into the
restored gate (not #928's separate gate file):

- Incompatible-ledger fail-closed: verify introspects ledger columns and fails
  closed with a structured "migration ledger validation failed" result (instead
  of an uncaught column-level SQL traceback) when the ledger schema is not this
  gate's native {version,filename,checksum_sha256,success} set, or when ledger
  inspection raises an unexpected DB error.
- No-mutate guard: apply refuses to mutate a pre-existing foreign ledger
  ("legacy migration ledger cannot be mutated by this gate").
- connect() wraps psycopg2 driver errors as a structured "database connection
  failed" fail-closed result (aligned with #928), surfaced by a packaged-image
  smoke test.

#917's {"status":"pass"|"fail-closed"} envelope and exit 0/2 are preserved;
#928's status strings/exit 1 were deliberately not adopted.

Adds docs/90-adr/adr-conport-migration-foundation-gate.md documenting the gate
decision, the #932 clobber+restore, and the ported hardening.

Validation:
- PASS: pytest gate suite 28/28 (20 #917 + 8 new hardening tests)
- PASS: docker compose build conport (gate + migrations packaged into image)
- PASS: in-container packaged-gate verify fails closed structured (exit 2)
- PASS: markdown-location-guard (ADR + proof md)
- NOT_RUN: in-container verify against a live applied Postgres (positive path)

